<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico completed participation whereby it had sought to drain 1.055 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday, through three direct sales of Cetes and two repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    335 days   23.00 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    181 days   21.75 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days   20.58 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    400 million     49 days   19.75 pct</p>
<p>    205 million	4 days   18.00 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
